# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Devora frontend — environment reference
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (Next.js loads it automatically and it is gitignored)
# and fill in real values. NEVER commit the filled-in file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Backend ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Where this frontend reaches the Devora API. Server-side only — the browser
# never sees this value. Requests go to `/backend/...` and Next rewrites them
# to this origin, so the browser stays same-origin and no CORS is involved.
#
#   dev  : http://127.0.0.1:8787
#   prod : https://api.<your-domain>    (or the internal address when the
#          frontend and backend share a box)
BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8787

# --- Clerk (authentication) -------------------------------------------------
# BOTH keys are needed, and the reason is worth knowing: `clerkMiddleware` in
# src/proxy.ts runs on the server and verifies sessions. That verification uses
# the secret. It is not read by any client code — Next only inlines
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` into the browser bundle, so the secret stays server-side.
#
# The backend holds its own copy of the same secret for API token checks. Both
# services verifying against the same Clerk instance is what makes one session
# work for the page and the API at once.
#
#   dev  : pk_test_... / sk_test_...
#   prod : pk_live_... / sk_live_...
#
# The prefix is what selects the Clerk instance, and nothing else in the code
# depends on which one it is — moving to production is these two values and
# nothing else. Note that dev and prod instances hold entirely separate user
# records; accounts created against one do not exist in the other.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
